# ModWrench environment configuration.
# Copy to `.env` at the workspace root and set only what you need.
#
# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ ModWrench NEVER reads a credential from this file.                       │
# │                                                                          │
# │ Your platform tokens / API keys live ONLY in your OS credential          │
# │ manager — Windows Credential Manager, macOS Keychain, or Linux           │
# │ libsecret — under service `modwrench-<platform>`, account `default`.     │
# │ ModWrench reads them from there, sends them, and keeps them no longer    │
# │ than the request that uses them. It never writes them during normal      │
# │ operation and never stores them on disk.                                 │
# │                                                                          │
# │ Store a credential yourself, or use the optional `modwrench auth login   │
# │ <platform>` helper, which deposits an OAuth token into your OS           │
# │ credential manager (still your store — ModWrench only reads it).         │
# │                                                                          │
# │ Everything below is NON-SECRET operational config only.                  │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘


# ─── Logging ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Minimum log level. One of: debug, info, warn, error. Default: info.
# Logs are written to stderr as JSON so they never interfere with MCP stdio
# traffic on stdout.
# LOG_LEVEL=debug


# ─── API base-URL overrides (non-secret) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Override only if you need to point at a proxy or a non-default endpoint.
# NEXUS_BASE_URL=https://api.nexusmods.com/v1
# MODIO_BASE_URL=https://api.mod.io/v1


# ─── Workbench ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Override Steam root detection if your Steam install isn't at one of the
# standard locations. Use forward slashes on Windows.
# Examples:
#   Windows:  D:/SteamLibrary
#   Linux:    /home/you/.steam/steam
#   macOS:    /Users/you/Library/Application Support/Steam
# STEAM_ROOT=

# Which branch of the LOOT masterlist repos to fetch from GitHub.
# Default: v0.26. Override to "master" for bleeding-edge masterlist data.
# Affects `mw_check_known_conflicts` for Bethesda games only.
# LOOT_BRANCH=

# Nexus tags some mods as adult content. Nexus requires third-party tools to
# filter what they return, so ModWrench drops adult-tagged results by default.
# Set this to true to receive them. This is intentionally an environment
# variable rather than a tool argument: only you can change it, not the AI.
# NEXUS_ALLOW_ADULT_CONTENT=true
